& [ConstraintGrounding] passes
  + user sources ground stored procedures, model-created procedures, Simula-inspired process control, shared SOP-mediated inference, and possible FPGA realization
  + inherited CTPR authority grounds immutable semantic repository, logical time, Calendar, Planner, tandem lanes, reflection, compiler walk, and fail-closed proof semantics
  + completed pure forms ground the available versioned machine ABI but not runtime correctness
  + framework governance grounds source preservation, delineation, SJS traces, support mapping, signatures, and phase locks
  + external technology evidence informs feasibility but grants no Cantor authority

& [GovernanceConstraints] are hard
  + CRPF-C001 raw source snapshots and manifests remain immutable and separate from derived artifacts
  + CRPF-C002 inherited CTPR authority cannot be widened by restatement
  + CRPF-C003 runtime, process procedure, and FPGA profile require distinguishable canonical identities and signatures
  + CRPF-C004 a signature binds exact artifact paths, hashes, requirement set, authority grade, and invalidation rules
  + CRPF-C005 no implementation begins from source, assessment, explosion, refinement, data design, justification, plan, or registry alone
  + CRPF-C006 current work stops before Rust runtime, parser, compiler, interpreter, HDL, HLS, synthesis, bitstream, or hardware behavior
  + CRPF-C007 later implementation requires a separate claim even after a valid signature
  + CRPF-C008 future source or locked-artifact drift invalidates the applicable signature without rewriting history

& [DeterminismConstraints] are hard
  + CRPF-C009 all first-proof time is supplied logical or fixture civil time
  + CRPF-C010 stable ordering is declared for maps, sets, graphs, events, messages, traces, and serialization
  + CRPF-C011 identical normalized inputs under the same exact profiles yield identical normalized results and semantic traces
  + CRPF-C012 no randomness, clock, environment, locale default, thread schedule, hash iteration, filesystem order, provider, or network response influences results
  + CRPF-C013 every collection, graph, recurrence, event queue, process set, step sequence, trace, text, and byte value has a finite bound
  + CRPF-C014 resource exhaustion returns a typed refusal or fault without partial admission
  + CRPF-C015 replay begins from an exact state digest and operation sequence
  + CRPF-C016 determinism cannot be used as evidence of semantic truth, safety, or completeness

& [RuntimeConstraints] are hard
  + CRPF-C017 FakeRepository preserves production-grade identity and transition invariants while remaining in memory
  + CRPF-C018 compare-and-append rejects stale or inconsistent predecessor state
  + CRPF-C019 snapshots declare semantic frontier and never claim simultaneous external-world state
  + CRPF-C020 indexes remain replaceable projections
  + CRPF-C021 Calendar schedule, commitment, provider sync, notification, and execution remain distinct
  + CRPF-C022 wake evaluation revalidates every pinned identity and authority input
  + CRPF-C023 Planner proposes and cannot admit, commit, authorize, or execute
  + CRPF-C024 dependency cycles and unresolved required identities fail with witnesses
  + CRPF-C025 simulated execution observation is input data and not an effect

& [TandemAndCompilerConstraints] are hard
  + CRPF-C026 lane state is immutable and version-pinned
  + CRPF-C027 missing, stale, wrong-generation, or wrong-subject returns never satisfy a join
  + CRPF-C028 timeout and lag are logical transitions and never background timers
  + CRPF-C029 release barriers name exact required receipts rather than counts
  + CRPF-C030 forward compiler prediction and rear correspondence checking are independently implemented and evidenced
  + CRPF-C031 checked status requires complete declared diff classes and explicit unknowns
  + CRPF-C032 bounded fixture evidence cannot support a general compiler or target claim

& [ProcedureLanguageConstraints] are hard
  + CRPF-C033 procedure source is Cantor Process Procedure, not vintage Simula compatibility
  + CRPF-C034 every type, schema, state, process, message, event, transition, fault, effect, and budget is explicit
  + CRPF-C035 implicit pointers, global state, native captured stacks, dynamic allocation, code loading, unrestricted inheritance, reflection, and self-modification are prohibited
  + CRPF-C036 loops, maps, waits, events, processes, messages, and call depth are bounded
  + CRPF-C037 procedure state changes only by immutable successor records
  + CRPF-C038 serialized continuation is validated exact state rather than opaque runtime state
  + CRPF-C039 canonical IR is backend- and provider-independent
  + CRPF-C040 source normalization, compilation, verification, and replay are deterministic
  + CRPF-C041 an effectless procedure reads only supplied typed input and pinned admitted in-memory artefacts
  + CRPF-C042 compilation does not imply verification, admission, catalogue insertion, invocation, or truth

& [AuthorityAndSecurityConstraints] are hard
  + CRPF-C043 model authorship grants no signing, admission, persistence, invocation, capability, or effect authority
  + CRPF-C044 proposal, validation, compilation, verification, admission, catalogue insertion, invocation, revocation, and effect mediation have distinct receipts and principals
  + CRPF-C045 every SOP anchor binds exact recognized identity, version, digest, intended use, and sensitivity
  + CRPF-C046 stale procedure, compiler, verifier, policy, schema, SOP, catalogue, participant, frame, or invocation generation fails closed
  + CRPF-C047 revocation prevents future invocation while preserving audit history
  + CRPF-C048 aliases, names, majority, consensus, low latency, and successful compilation never replace exact authority
  + CRPF-C049 secrets, credentials, hardware keys, and private chain-of-thought are prohibited first-profile inputs
  + CRPF-C050 input and output sensitivity propagate through messages, traces, results, and retention

& [SharedInferenceConstraints] are hard
  + CRPF-C051 every participant is named with role and permitted message kinds
  + CRPF-C052 shared perspective is a versioned negotiated frame and message log rather than mutable shared attention
  + CRPF-C053 one complete unchanged token cycle requires the exact participant set and exact frame generation
  + CRPF-C054 silence, timeout, absence, stale pass, or tool failure is not assent
  + CRPF-C055 frame, participant, SOP-anchor, policy, proposal, objection, or qualification change invalidates earlier incomplete pass sets
  + CRPF-C056 agreement cannot by itself establish truth, evidence, permission, or Observer admission
  + CRPF-C057 model interaction uses explicit structured tool boundaries across multiple inference passes
  + CRPF-C058 no claim of direct K/V cache, hidden-state, weight, or uninterrupted-forward-pass sharing is permitted

& [FPGATargetConstraints] are hard for the profile
  + CRPF-C059 FPGA is an optional derived backend, not the SOP or process source language
  + CRPF-C060 only effectless finite bounded canonical IR subsets are eligible
  + CRPF-C061 profiling and a measured software baseline precede native lowering authority
  + CRPF-C062 interpreter and native realizations retain different identities, evidence, and admission
  + CRPF-C063 physical cycles may vary while normalized semantic trace and typed result must correspond
  + CRPF-C064 toolchain, device, board, constraints, clock, interface, resources, timing, netlist, and bitstream are absent until a target-specific addendum
  + CRPF-C065 source admission, software admission, hardware compilation, bitstream signing, and device loading are distinct authorities
  + CRPF-C066 model-generated HDL, HLS, constraints, or bitstreams cannot self-verify, self-sign, or self-load
  + CRPF-C067 hardware acceleration cannot be represented as semantic accuracy improvement without separate evidence

& [ProofConstraints] are hard
  + CRPF-C068 every requirement maps to source pressure, refined meaning, data support, canonical clause, acceptance, and future proof status
  + CRPF-C069 positive and negative acceptance criteria cover every lifecycle and authority edge
  + CRPF-C070 software and future hardware correspondence compares normalized semantic traces, not only final scalar output
  + CRPF-C071 known limitations, residual uncertainty, unsupported versions, and deferred features remain explicit
  + CRPF-C072 a phase lock records no implementation evidence that does not exist

& [ConstraintReapplicationTrace] passes current derived artifacts
  + runtime explosion preserves C001 through C032, C043 through C050, C068 through C072
  + procedure explosion preserves C001 through C016, C033 through C058, C068 through C072
  + FPGA explosion preserves C001 through C008, C039, C043 through C050, C059 through C072
  + semantic refinement repairs the false equivalences named by C016, C042, C048, C056, C058, C059, C063, C065, and C067
